# promo-replacements.tsv — exact sentence replacements for the expired 15% food promo.
# Tab-separated: <exact text found on the page><TAB><exact replacement>. Empty replacement deletes.
# Written by hand against the issuer's rate table (help.ether.fi/en/articles/262374, read 2026-08-13):
#   Core     3% on the first $2,000/mo, 1% to $3,000, 0.5% above
#   Luxe     3% on the first $10,000/mo, 1% to $20,000, 0.5% above
#   Pinnacle 3% on the first $50,000/mo, 1% to $80,000, 0.5% above
#   Business 1% flat. NO merchant-category bonuses of any kind.
# Longest / most specific entries first, so a short entry cannot eat part of a long one.
The 3% standard cashback rate plus 15% limited-time promo on dining creates an effective 4–6% return on typical travel spending (hotels, food, local merchants), while the $40 refundable physical-card deposit is returned to your account—not a fee.	The 3% rate on the first band of monthly spend gives a solid return on typical travel spending (hotels, food, local merchants); note the physical card costs $50 on Core and the issuer does not call it refundable.
A user spending $2,000/month on groceries (15% promo) + $1,500 on standard purchases (3% base) earns ~$1,440/year in cashback — enough to justify a $50 annual Pinnacle upgrade fee if they exceed spending caps.	A Core member spending $2,000/month earns 3% across that whole band — about $720/year — with the rate stepping down to 1% and then 0.5% on anything spent above it.
The combination of 0% FX on USD, 3% base cashback, and 15% food rewards makes ether.fi Cash the highest-value option for typical Pennsylvania spending patterns ($2,000–$3,000/month).	At $2,000–$3,000/month, a Pennsylvania spender earns 3% on the first $2,000 and 1% on the rest, so the effective rate falls as spending rises past the first band.
ether.fi, by contrast, offers [consistent up to 3% cashback](<<AFFILIATE_URL>>) on all spend, with seasonal promotions boosting dining/groceries to 15%.	ether.fi, by contrast, offers [up to 3% cashback](<<AFFILIATE_URL>>) on the first band of monthly spend, stepping down to 1% and then 0.5% above it.
Similarly, the promotional **15 %** cashback on food is time-limited and applies only to eligible merchants; after the promotion expires, users revert to the base **3 %** rate.	Similarly, the **3 %** rate applies only to the first band of monthly spend; above it the rate steps down to **1 %** and then **0.5 %**.
