Leading cards offer 1–3 % cashback on everyday purchases and promotional rates up to 15 % on specific categories (dining, groceries, travel).	Leading cards offer 1–3 % cashback on everyday purchases, and most step the rate down as monthly spend rises.
**ether.fi Cash on Amazon:** You get 3% cashback on all purchases (Amazon isn't "dining/groceries", so the 15% promo doesn't apply).	**ether.fi Cash on Amazon:** You get 3% cashback on the first band of your monthly spend. ether.fi has no merchant-category bonuses, so Amazon earns exactly what any other merchant earns.
Top up before your planned grocery, restaurant, or dining purchases to capture ether.fi's up-to-15% promo cashback in those categories.	Top up before large purchases early in the month, while your spend is still inside the 3% band.
ether.fi's 3% standard plus 15% food, plus zero annual fee, means **you keep 1–2% more per transaction**—or **$100–$200 per year** on $10k annual spend.	ether.fi's 3% on the first spend band, plus zero annual fee, means **you keep more on the first $2,000 you spend each month** — after which the rate steps down.
**3% cashback is simple & consistent:** No category limits, no time windows—every purchase earns back 3%, with dining bonuses up to 15%.	**3% cashback with no category rules:** every merchant earns the same rate. What changes is volume — 3% on the first band of monthly spend, then 1%, then 0.5%.
